error[E0403]: expected Sender<Holder>, found Sender<Holder>
   --> tests/programs/concurrency/actors/state_or_handle.la:11:12
   |
11 |     h.keep(tx);
   |            ^^ expected Sender<Holder>
   |
   = help: two types are named `Holder` here: inside `actor Holder`'s body the name means its state, so the code expects its state but has a handle to it; the actor's handle type can't be written inside its body

For more about E0403, run `lughac explain E0403`.
